@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: WWW Resource Library
	Frontend testing for the www resource library page

Scenario: Filter Resources By Type
	End users should be able to filter resources by type and view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the relative url "resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Types | Whitepapers |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "Whitepaper"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Case Studies"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
#	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Product Info"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Types | Case Studies |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "Case Studies"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Whitepaper"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Product Info"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Types | E-books |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Case Studies"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Whitepaper"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Product Info"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Types | Product Info |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "Product Info"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Case Studies"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Types | Research Reports |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Product Info"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Case Studies"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Whitepaper"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Types | Whitepapers |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view a resource with the type "Whitepaper"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Case Studies"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "E-books"
	And I should not be able to view a resource with the type "Research Reports"

Scenario: Filter Resources By Solution
	End users should be able to filter resources by solution and view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the relative url "resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solutions | Customer Portals |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "The Evolving Value of a Portal"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "What is a Portal"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Portal Best Practices"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solutions | Intranets |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Building a Better, More Secure Collaborative Platform for Researchers"
#	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "The Evolving Value of a Portal"
#	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "What is a Portal"
#	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Portal Best Practices"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solutions | B2B Commerce |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "7 Best Practices for B2B Ecommerce Success"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "How to Use Your E-Commerce Site to Empower Your Sales Team"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "B2B E-Commerce RFP Kit"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "B2BecNews Report - Choosing the Right E-Commerce Platform"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Building a Better, More Secure Collaborative Platform for Researchers"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solutions | Websites |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Public website gives access to new mobile audience with responsive design"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "7 Best Practices for B2B Ecommerce Success"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "How to Use Your E-Commerce Site to Empower Your Sales Team"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "B2B E-Commerce RFP Kit"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "B2BecNews Report - Choosing the Right E-Commerce Platform"

Scenario: Filter Resources By Industries
	End users should be able to filter resources by industries and view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the relative url "resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Industries | Manufacturing |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "100,000 users united through a self-service portal, simplifying incident management"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "A Coordinated Commerce Strategy for B2B Companies"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Industries | Healthcare |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Transforming the Pharma and Life Sciences Industry"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "The Evolving Value of the Portal in Healthcare"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Healthcare Insurer Delivers Streamlined Digital Experience for Customers and Employees"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "100,000 users united through a self-service portal, simplifying incident management"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "A Coordinated Commerce Strategy for B2B Companies"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Industries | Government |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Government: Department of the Citizen - Australia"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "A new intranet for the US Navy serves 40,000 users with exceptional performance and user satisfaction"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Digital Transformation in the UK Public Sector"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Council of Europe creates effective communication tool with Liferay Portal"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Transforming the Pharma and Life Sciences Industry"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "The Evolving Value of the Portal in Healthcare"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Healthcare Insurer Delivers Streamlined Digital Experience for Customers and Employees"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Industries | Not For Profit/NGO |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Public website gives access to new mobile audience with responsive design"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Government: Department of the Citizen - Australia"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "A new intranet for the US Navy serves 40,000 users with exceptional performance and user satisfaction"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Digital Transformation in the UK Public Sector"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Council of Europe creates effective communication tool with Liferay Portal"

Scenario: Filter Resources Using Multiple Criteria
	End users should be able to filter resources by multiple criteria and view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the relative url "resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solutions      | Websites      |
	| Industries     | Government    |
	| Resource Types | Case Studies  |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "New platform skyrockets search usage"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solutions      | Customer Portals |
	| Industries     | Manufacturing    |
	| Resource Types | Case Studies     |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Agricultural Equipment Manufacturer Doubles Site Visitors"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "New platform skyrockets search usage"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solutions      | B2B Commerce     |
	| Industries     | Manufacturing    |
	| Resource Types | Research Reports |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Why Customer Centricity is Essential to Manufacturers"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Agricultural Equipment Manufacturer Doubles Site Visitors"
	When I clear all resource filters
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solutions      | Websites           |
	| Industries     | Financial Services |
	| Resource Types | Case Studies       |
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Leading Financial Services Company Publishes Content and Code Faster with Liferay"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Integrated portal platform at center of Britam"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Why Customer Centricity is Essential to Manufacturers"

Scenario: Search Resources By Keyword
	End users should be able to search for resources by keyword and view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the relative url "resources"
	And I type in the resource keyword "Portal" in the Resource Library search bar and click search
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "The Evolving Value of a Portal"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "What is a Portal"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Portal Best Practices"
	When I reset the search bar
	And I type in the resource keyword "Digital Transformation" in the Resource Library search bar and click search
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Jumpstart Your Digital Transformation With a Digital Experience Platform"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Building Trust in Government Through Digital Transformation"
#	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "The Evolving Value of a Portal"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "What is a Portal"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Portal Best Practices"
	When I reset the search bar
	And I type in the resource keyword "E-Commerce" in the Resource Library search bar and click search
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "7 Best Practices for B2B Ecommerce Success"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "How to Use Your E-Commerce Site to Empower Your Sales Team"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "B2B E-Commerce RFP Kit"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "B2BecNews Report - Choosing the Right E-Commerce Platform"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Jumpstart Your Digital Transformation With a Digital Experience Platform"
#	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Building Trust in Government Through Digital Transformation"
	When I reset the search bar
	And I type in the resource keyword "Customer Experience" in the Resource Library search bar and click search
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Leveraging AI to Improve the B2B Customer Experience"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Four Strategies to Transform Your Customer Experience"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Liferay DXP Business Overview"
	And I should be able to view the resource with the title "Three Key Strategies for Consistent Customer Experiences"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "7 Best Practices for B2B Ecommerce Success"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "How to Use Your E-Commerce Site to Empower Your Sales Team"
#	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "The B2B E-Commerce RFP Kit"
#	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "B2BecNews Report - Choosing the Right E-Commerce Platform"

Scenario: Filter and Search for Resources
	End users should be able to filter and search for resources view the results accordingly.

	Given I go to the www page with the relative url "resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Solutions      | Partner Portals |
	| Resource Types | E-books         |
	And I type in the resource keyword "Liferay DXP" in the Resource Library search bar and click search
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Five Ways Liferay DXP Enables Success for Insurance Providers"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Conquering 6 Common Challenges With an Engaging Digital Agent Portal"
	When I reset the search bar
	And I type in the resource keyword "Digital Agent Portal" in the Resource Library search bar and click search
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Conquering 6 Common Challenges With an Engaging Digital Agent Portal"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Five Ways Liferay DXP Enables Success for Insurance Providers"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Seven Popular Liferay Use Cases"
	When I reset the search bar
	And I type in the resource keyword "Four types of Portals" in the Resource Library search bar and click search
	And I toggle the results per page value to "90" results
	Then I should be able to view the resource with the title "Four Types of Portals That Solve Enterprise Problems"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Conquering 6 Common Challenges With an Engaging Digital Agent Portal"
	And I should not be able to view the resource with the title "Five Ways Liferay DXP Enables Success for Insurance Providers"

Scenario: Download e-book resource via resources form
	End users should be able to request a download of e-book resource via resources form.

	Given I go to the www page with the relative url "resources"
	And I filter the resources in the Resource Library using the following filters and values
	| Resource Types | E-books |
	And I click on the resource with the title "5 Ways to Use Customer Engagement to Increase Profitability"
	Then I should be able to view the resources form
	And I request a download of a resource with the following values
	| Work Email                         | usr.resources1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Country                            | United States                        |
	| State/Territory                    | California                           |
	| First Name                         | USR                                  |
	| Last Name                          | Resources1                           |
	| Company                            | Reusr                                |
	#Necessary pause for the download to complete
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	And I should see the downloaded file "5 Ways Customer Engagement Increases Profitability.pdf"
	And the current url content should contain the text "resources/thank-you"

